Plain-English summary (NON-BINDING — the Parameters above and the Terms below
are what legally govern; this is here only to save you reading legalese):

elifant is SOURCE-AVAILABLE. You can read every line, run it, fork it, and
BUILD ON IT. You may use it in production, for free, if ANY of these is true:

  * You EMBED it in an application you ship — your users get it as part of your
    product. (This is the common case: build your thing on elifant.)
  * You use it PERSONALLY or for non-commercial work.
  * Your ORGANIZATION runs it internally and is small — fewer than 5 deployments
    in aggregate, OR under $1,000,000/yr in revenue.

The ONE thing that needs a commercial license is offering elifant ITSELF to
third parties as a hosted/managed service, library, or product — i.e.
repackaging the engine as a competing service — or running it past the
thresholds above.

So: build freely on top of elifant. Just don't resell elifant as a service. And
on the Change Date (2030-05-22) the whole thing converts to Apache 2.0 anyway.

Commercial license / questions: steve@mediagato.com

